# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=LoRaWAN
Version=v2.5.0_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
STM32WL5MXX|Module|Application selection||||
SUBGHZ_APPLICATION|Application|Application selection||||List of available applications
DISPLAY_APPLICATION|Application|Application selection||||List of available applications, some available starting the new project from EXAMPLE SELECTOR other from MCU or BOARD SELECTOR
DEBUGGER_ON|Serial Wires or JTAG enabled|Application selection||||
UTIL_SEQ_EN_M4|Use Sequencer kernel on CM4|Application selection||||
UTIL_SEQ_EN_M0|Use Sequencer kernel on CM0|Application selection||||
UTIL_TIMER_EN|Enable/Disable TIMER utility|Application selection||||
LORAWAN_KMS|Use KMS for LoRaWAN|Application selection||||enable KMS for LoRa code, forbidden
DEBUG_SUBGHZSPI_MONITORING|Sub-GHz radio SPI interface|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_NRESET|Sub-GHz radio NRESET|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_HSE32RDY|Sub-GHz radio HSE32 CLOCK monitoring|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_SMPSRDY|Sub-GHz radio SMPS ready monitoring|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_LDORDY|Sub-GHz radio LDO ready monitoring|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_DTB1|Sub-GHz radio Internal Signal monitoring|Application selection||||
DEBUG_RF_BUSY|Sub-GHz radio Busy monitoring|Application selection||||
FILL_UCS|Fill User Code Sections|Application selection||||
USE_LPM|Configure Low Power Mode|Application selection||||Allow pre-fill of stm32_lpm_if.c file.
USE_ADC|Use ADC for T° and battery management|Application selection||||<font color="blue"><b>ADC:</b> Proposed solution to manage radio settings depending on Vrefint and device internal T°.</font>    • For Dual Core operation Runtime Context is Cortex-M4 <b>Mode:</b> Temperature Sensor Channel and Vrefint Channel <b>Configuration:</b> - Parameters Settings:    • Clock Prescaler: Synchronous clock mode divided by 4    • Overrun behaviour: Overrun data overwritten    • SamplingTime Common 1 and 2: 160.5 Cycles <font color="blue"><b>LoRaWAN - Platform Settings panel:</b> Platform proposals</font>    • Ensure that ADC is selected in Found Solutions
USE_RTC|Use RTC for Timer|Application selection||||<font color="blue"><b>RTC:</b> Proposed solution to manage timer in Low Power mode.</font>    • For Dual Core operation Runtime Contexts are both Cortex-M4 and Cortex-M0+ and initializer is Cortex-M0+ <b>Mode:</b> Activate Clock Source, Activate Calendar and activate Alarm A (and B for Dual Core) (Internal Alarm A (and B for Dual Core)) <b>User Constants:</b> Add the following Constants    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_N_PREDIV_S</b> Value: 10    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_PREDIV_S</b> Value: ((1 &lt;&lt; RTC_N_PREDIV_S)-1)    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_PREDIV_A</b> Value: ((1 &lt;&lt; (15-RTC_N_PREDIV_S))-1) <b>Configuration</b> - Parameters Settings:    • Asynchronous Predivider value: Set value to RTC_PREDIV_A    • Bin Mode: Free running Binary mode    • Alarm A Binary AutoControl: RTC_ALARMSUBSECONDBIN_AUTOCLR_NO <b>Configuration</b> - NVIC settings:    • Enable both Interrupts <font color="blue"><b>LoRaWAN - Platform Settings panel:</b> Platform proposals</font>    • Ensure that RTC is selected in Found Solutions
USE_UART|Use UART for Trace|Application selection||||<font color="blue"><b>USART/LPUART:</b> Proposed solution to manage trace.</font>    • For Dual Core operation Runtime Context is Cortex-M4 <b>Mode:</b> Asynchronous <b>Configuration</b> - Parameters Settings:    • If LPUART is selected then set Baud Rate: 9600 Bits/s <b>Configuration</b> - DMA Settings:    • Add USARTx_TX DMA Request with Channel configured with DMA1 Channel 5 <b>Configuration</b> - NVIC settings:    • Enable both Interrupts <b>Clock Configuration panel</b>    • If LPUART is selected then set Clock Mux to LSE <b>NVIC Mode and Configuration panel</b> - Preemption priority management    • Set preemption Priority for DMA and UART Interrupt to 2 <font color="blue"><b>LoRaWAN - Platform Settings panel:</b> Platform proposals</font>    • Ensure that chosen UART is selected in Found Solutions
USER_GUIDANCE_UTIL|none|Application selection||||<> If you see this message it means some Utilities are disabled. <> In this case only "User Defined Skeleton" Application is allowed. <> Please, enable all Utilities if you wish additional Application choices.
USER_GUIDANCE|Application configuration recommandations|Application selection||||<font color="blue"><b>KMS:</b> To set LoRaWAN using the KMS Middleware,</font><> <> User Code Sections in following files in the DualCore example project must be filled manually after generation:    • CM0PLUS/Core/Inc/kms_platf_objects_config.h : Add all LoRaWAN keys as kms_object_keyhead_32_t structures    • CM0PLUS/Core/Inc/kms_platf_objects_interface.h : Add all LoRaWAN key indexes    • CM0PLUS/Core/Inc/nvms_low_level.h : Enable the NVMS (Non Volatile Memory) to store the session keys    • CM0PLUS/Core/Src/nvms_low_level.c : Implement the Flash read/write functions to manage the NVMS items <> Example can be found in the RF projects in the STM32CubeWL MCU package : <> <font color="purple"> www.st.com/stm32cubewl</font> <font color="blue"><b>ADC:</b> Proposed solution to manage radio settings depending on Vrefint and device internal T°.</font>    • For Dual Core operation: Runtime Contexts is Cortex-M4 <b>Mode:</b> Temperature Sensor Channel and Vrefint Channel <b>Configuration:</b> - Parameters Settings:    • Clock Prescaler: Synchronous clock mode divided by 4    • Overrun behaviour: Overrun data overwritten    • SamplingTime Common 1 and 2: 160.5 Cycles <font color="blue"><b>RTC:</b> Proposed solution to manage timer in Low Power mode.</font>    • For Dual Core operation Runtime Contexts are both Cortex-M4 and Cortex-M0+ and initializer is Cortex-M0+ <b>Mode:</b> Activate Clock Source, Activate Calendar and activate Alarm A (and B for Dual Core) (Internal Alarm A (and B for Dual Core)) <b>User Constants:</b> Add the following Constants    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_N_PREDIV_S</b> Value: 10    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_PREDIV_S</b> Value: ((1 &lt;&lt; RTC_N_PREDIV_S)-1)    • Constant Name: <b>RTC_PREDIV_A</b> Value: ((1 &lt;&lt; (15-RTC_N_PREDIV_S))-1) <b>Configuration</b> - Parameters Settings:    • Asynchronous Predivider value: Set value to RTC_PREDIV_A    • Bin Mode: Free running Binary mode    • Alarm A Binary AutoControl: RTC_ALARMSUBSECONDBIN_AUTOCLR_NO <b>Configuration</b> - NVIC settings:    • Enable both Interrupts <font color="blue"><b>RCC:</b> Proposed solution to manage RCC.</font> <b>Mode:</b> Low Speed Clock (LSE): Set value to Crystal Ceramic Resonator <b>Configuration</b> - Parameters Settings:    • Flash Latency(WS): 2 WS (3 CPU cycle)    • Power Regulator Voltage Scale: Scale 1 <b>Clock Configuration panel</b>    • Set MSI RC to 32MHz    • Set RTC Clock Mux to LSE <font color="blue"><b>USART/LPUART:</b> Proposed solution to manage trace.</font>    • For Dual Core operation: Runtime Contexts is Cortex-M4 <b>Mode:</b> Asynchronous <b>Configuration</b> - Parameters Settings:    • If LPUART is selected then set Baud Rate: 9600 Bits/s <b>Configuration</b> - DMA Settings:    • Add USARTx_TX DMA Request with Channel configured with DMA1 Channel 5 <b>Configuration</b> - NVIC settings:    • Enable both Interrupts <b>Clock Configuration panel</b>    • If LPUART is selected then set Clock Mux to LSE <b>NVIC Mode and Configuration panel</b> - Preemption priority management    • Set preemption Priority for DMA and UART Interrupt to 2 <font color="blue"><b>LoRaWAN - Platform Settings panel:</b> Platform proposals</font>    • Ensure that relevant solutions are properly selected <font color="blue"><b>Project Manager- Advanced Settings panel:</b> Generated Function Calls management</font>    • Untick "Generate Code" for RTC on CortexM4 and DMA on CortexM0PLUS for Dual Core    • Tick "Do Not Generate Function Call" for DMA (CortexM4 only for DualCore), ADC, RTC, SUBGHZ, UART and IPCC(for Dual Core)    • Untick Visibility for all Function Calls on both cores
